{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790979352,"nonce":"/990Hqzkj9qyBlkVN1rEJZRBsks=","title":"xgpu descriptors register under gpu:: while the externs declare rayzor::gpu::","message":"gpu/build.rs calls x-idl's `generate_rayzor_with_resources(\"gpu\", ...)`, which names each XIDL_METHODS table class by the Rust namespace: `gpu::GpuDevice`. The generated Haxe externs are in package `rayzor.gpu` with `@:native(\"rayzor::gpu::GpuDevice\")`. Descriptors match classes by exact name, so every xgpu descriptor registers a class nothing uses. Methods work only because the bodyless `@:native` extern methods are registered from the Haxe files, so a descriptor and its extern can disagree unnoticed.\n\nFix, once x-idl pushes it (x-idl git-bug b0b5a118a997f830d9fb6419d75dafe64069ce407b2aa07e84ec3e1cb4a69659): call `generate_rayzor_in(\"gpu\", \"rayzor.gpu\", ...)` (directly via x_idl, or through xgpu_bindgen's re-export once updated), which names table classes `package.replace('.', \"::\")`. Then check the descriptors reach the extern classes, and whether compiler_plugin's lookup relied on the `gpu::` names. The same x-idl push takes declarations as text (`impl Into\u003cx_idl::Declaration\u003e`, x-idl 42259f6), so build.rs no longer needs a temporary declaration file.","files":null}]}